---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Cookie policy"
  description="What cookies and similar browser storage the DPEEN website uses, and how to control them."
>
  <p>
    Cookies are small files that websites place on your device. Some sites use
    them to track you across the web. This one does not. This policy lists
    everything the DPEEN website stores in your browser so you can see for
    yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Cookies we set</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>None.</strong> The DPEEN website does not set cookies of its own,
    and it does not load advertising, analytics or social media tracking tools.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Other browser storage we use</h2>
  <p>
    The site uses two small pieces of browser storage that work like cookies.
    Both are needed to provide the site you asked for, so we do not ask for
    consent first.
  </p>
  <div class="legal-table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Name</th>
          <th scope="col">What it does</th>
          <th scope="col">How long</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>
            <code>dpeen-notice</code> (local storage)
          </td>
          <td>Remembers that you dismissed the cookie notice.</td>
          <td>Until you clear your browser data</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Offline cache (service worker)</td>
          <td>
            Saves copies of the site’s pages, images and styles so it loads
            faster and still opens with a weak connection.
          </td>
          <td>Refreshed whenever we publish an update</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>3. Third-party requests</h2>
  <p>
    When a page loads, your browser fetches the typeface from Google Fonts and
    some photographs from Unsplash. When we last checked on 22 October 2026,
    these requests did not set cookies. Even so, those companies can see your IP
    address and browser details, as any website you visit can. Our{' '}
    <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> explains this in more detail.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Controlling storage</h2>
  <p>
    You can block or delete cookies and site data in your browser settings. The
    site still works if you do. If you clear site data, the cookie notice will
    appear again on your next visit.
  </p>

  <h2>5. If this changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever add analytics or other tools that use cookies, we will update
    this page first and ask for your consent before they run. Questions? Email{' '}
    <a href="mailto:info@dpeenetwork.com">info@dpeenetwork.com</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
